{"parentUuid":"24e5c3cb-77e8-4893-aee9-a1f79c7bf95d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgww6F9nEQQqPTyvvHPzY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Evals and Verification now offer \"All servers\", and an eval's page charts A against B. Both changes are pushed: U5 (`b9f754d`) and U6 (`6fd90f5`). The earlier U1–U4 push passed CI on both runners. CI on these two has not finished yet.\n\n**What I took \"lives there too\" to mean:** Evals, Costs and Verification can show every server at once. All three stay as tabs in the bar, so they're still one click away.\n\n**U5, Evals and Verification across servers**\n- Each eval and each landed job names its server, and clicking one opens it on that server.\n- A new eval runs on the last single server you picked, and the form says which: \"Run an eval on local\".\n- An escape report goes to whichever server landed that commit, so you can report from \"All servers\".\n- `two` has no evals and no landed jobs yet, so live I could only see `local`'s rows on these pages. Tests cover the merge.\n\n**U6, A against B on an eval's page**\n- One chart covers the totals: grade, cost, seconds, turns, calls, refused, held and flagged. Each measure shows A and B as two bars and says how B differs from A.\n- Grade, cost, time, turns and calls are colored green or red for better or worse. Refused, held and flagged stay neutral, because an enforced rung is meant to raise them.\n- A second chart compares each request's grade under A and B.\n- Live, on \"no-wc told vs enforced\": B cost 40% less, took 25% less time, 28% fewer turns and 48% fewer calls. It refused 5 calls where A refused 0, and both graded 7.\n- Two bugs from the live run are fixed: a change from zero read \"same\", and a zero still drew a thin bar.\n\n**Also done:**\n- The local dev server stopped when its background task hit its time limit. I restarted it detached, so it doesn't depend on my session.\n- A per-step budget (most revisions, most spend) is now in PLAN.md, next to the per-step model.\n\n**Next in PLAN.md.** Each item changes the core, so I'd write a decision for each first:\n1. A model and a budget per step. This is the smallest: a few step fields, used when a step's turn starts and when it asks for a revision.\n2. Step names as `workflow/step`, with constraints and capabilities set per workflow step. This changes D42 and how the gate looks up rules.\n3. Workflows that branch: a step can name the step to go to on failure.\n\nI'd start with 1. Should I go ahead?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_read_input_tokens":600667,"output_tokens":1002,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":191},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":315,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1002,"cache_read_input_tokens":600667,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":315},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b2b05f2e-e732-41e4-b640-c0f83f8386e2","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgww6EZo9AeaVTa94YP92","type":"assistant","uuid":"4e8853f5-4b15-4833-8b92-6b463bbb7f07","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:31:27.221Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
