{"parentUuid":"3fd38de6-1f5b-4366-bdac-136f8771bc81","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx4meV8JafXEgkCM84kM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both are done.\n\n1. **Test workflows:** \"Short, options test\", \"Command test\" and \"Branch test\" are deleted from `local`. Their earlier versions stay in the history, as with any deleted workflow, so the test jobs can still show what they ran. The test commit in `demo-local` is still there, since it's only my scratch repo; say if you want it gone.\n2. **`bastion-gh` charter:** I moved `.claude/settings.json` and `.claude/check.sh` into `.agents/`, and pointed the hook at `sh .agents/check.sh`. I also reworded a comment in `check.sh` that named Claude Code. There was no `CLAUDE.md`, so no `AGENTS.md` was needed. I committed it on `main` in `~/Code/bastion` as `50558a4`, but didn't push it. The server now reads that charter: the `git push` deny rule, the check hook before shell commands, and `pytest` when a build ends.\n\nWhat should the next plan cover?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":359,"cache_read_input_tokens":855328,"output_tokens":323,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":359,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":323,"cache_read_input_tokens":855328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":359},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"1d4da1f3-c72c-4ea3-8af7-91058e584975","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgx4mdGwSevPs4uaRahSf","type":"