 grant, and a refusal names the step\"\n        );\n        assert_eq!(\n            at(\"short/build\"),\n            Decision::Continue,\n            \"the kind's at another step\"\n        );\n        assert_eq!(at(\"\"), Decision::Continue, \"no step named\");\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn a_constraint_for_some_steps_binds_only_there() {\n        let rule = Constraint {\n            id: \"no-rm\".into(),\n            rule: \"Do not delete.\".into(),\n203:fn grant_for<'a>(call: &Call, at: At, grants: &'a [Capability]) -> Option<&'a Capability> {\n204-    let At { stage, step } = at;\n205-    let fits = |g: &&Capability| {\n206-        let here = (g.step.is_empty() && g.stage == stage) || (!step.is_empty() && g.step == step);\n207-        here && matches(&g.function, &call.function)\n208-    };\n209-    grants.iter().filter(fits).max_by_key(|g| {\n210-        (\n211-            !g.step.is_empty(),\n212-            !g.function.ends_with('*'),\n213-            g.function.len(),\n214-        )\n215-    })\n216-}\n217-\n218-/// Judge one call at `step`, named `workflow/step`, of kind `stage`. A\n219-/// write to the charter is refused first, then any call an enforced","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"17cb29a4-a4a2-482b-8f41-e737fc3d9bba","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:13:46.229Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"        );\n        assert_eq!(\n            Enforcement::Enforced.demote().demote().demote(),\n            Enforcement::Told\n        );\n        assert_eq!(\n            Access::Denied.promote().promote().promote(),\n            Access::Allowed\n        );\n        assert_eq!(Access::Allowed.demote().demote().demote(), Access::Denied);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn a_denied_grant_refuses() {\n        let grants = [Capability {\n            stage: Stage::Prompt,\n            step: String::new(),\n            function: \"sandbox::exec\".into(),\n            rung: Access::Denied,\n        }];\n        let verdict = gate(&exec(\"ls\"), Stage::Prompt, &[],