{"parentUuid":"539f2398-2363-45ba-9a00-5dabbc0e6879","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx5HxzCgkX6RAUMWhdjX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Hda9TQYgDD7AL8XuDAwjVM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open('DECISIONS.md').read()\nlines=s.split('\\n')\ni=[k for k,l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| D47 |')][0]\nlines.insert(i+1,\"| D48 | A grant is ask or allowed; a call no grant covers is refused, so there is no denied grant. Demoting a grant from ask removes it. A step's own grants, when it has any, take the place of its kind's, so a step is narrowed by listing what it may call. This replaces D44's \\\"wins over its kind's\\\". |\")\nopen('DECISIONS.md','w').write('\\n'.join(lines))\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\nj=s.index('## Open questions')\ns=s[:j]+'''### U13. A step's rules on the workflows page (D48)\n\n- An agent's step shows its rules: the constraints that apply there, each\n  marked every step or scoped, with \"Not here\" and a picker to apply one\n  scoped to other steps here too; and its grants.\n- A step uses its kind's grants until \"Give this step its own grants\"\n  copies them as its own, which then take their place; \"Use its kind's\n  instead\" takes them back.\n- A grant is ask or allowed; demoting from ask removes it. Migration 8\n  drops denied grants and limits the rung to ask and allowed.\n\nDone 2026-11-11. Live, on Bug fix's build step: its own grants started as\na copy of the prompt kind's `sandbox::*` allowed, demoted to ask, then\nRemove took it back to the kind's; the audit recorded the grant, the\ndemotion and the removal. Taking a constraint off its only step is\nrefused, as that would apply it at every step.\n\n'''+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncargo fmt --all -- --check && scripts/check-seams.sh | tail -1 && CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A6 | head; CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo test --workspace 2>&1 | grep -E \"FAILED|panicked\"; git add PLAN.md DECISIONS.md crates","description":"Record D48 and U13; CI; stage","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":575,"cache_read_input_tokens":896384,"output_tokens":1043,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":24},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":575,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1043,"cache_read_input_tokens":896384,"cache_creation_input_tokens":575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":575},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Hda9TQYgDD7AL8XuDAwjVM":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open('DECISIONS.md').read()\nlines=s.split('\\n')\ni=[k for k,l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| D47 |')][0]\nlines.insert(i+1,\"| D48 | A grant is ask or allowed; a call no grant covers is refused, so there is no denied grant. Demoting a grant from ask removes it. A step's own grants, when it has any, take the place of its kind's, so a step is narrowed by listing what it may call. This replaces D44's \\\"wins over its kind's\\\". |\")\nopen('DECISIONS.md','w').write('\\n'.join(lines))\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\nj=s.index('## Open questions')\ns=s[:j]+'''### U13. A step's rules on the workflows page (D48)\n\n- An agent's step shows its rules: the constraints that apply there, each\n  marked every step or scoped, with \"Not here\" and a picker to apply one\n  scoped to other steps here too; and its grants.\n- A step uses its kind's grants until \"Give this step its own grants\"\n  copies them as its own, which then take their place; \"Use its kind's\n  instead\" takes them back.\n- A grant is ask or allowed; demoting from ask removes it. Migration 8\n  drops denied grants and limits the rung to ask and allowed.\n\nDone 2026-11-11. Live, on Bug fix's build step: its own grants started as\na copy of the prompt kind's `sandbox::*` allowed, demoted to ask, then\nRemove took it back to the kind's; the audit recorded the grant, the\ndemotion and the removal. Taking a constraint off its only step is\nrefused, as that would apply it at every step.\n\n'''+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncargo fmt --all -- --check && scripts/check-seams.sh | tail -1 && CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A6 | head; CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo test --workspace 2>&1 | grep -E \"FAILED|panicked\"; git add PLAN.md DECISIONS.md crates","description":"Record D48 and U13; CI; stage","timeout":600000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01Hda9TQYgDD7AL8XuDAwjVM":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d3543368-8938-4537-b9eb-b9a707bfca03","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgx5HxdNVkEbQpGNzArxM","type":"assistant","uuid":"54ca42f8-907b-4df8-ad4d-13dfd2e7a7ae","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:19:00.028Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
